DrawPad: the MNIST MLP and a 28x28 floor canvas in ONE DOOM map: 1,355 voodoo dolls, 89,063 sectors, 31,969 x 5,192 map units (built in 5 s).
You play in the DOOM window; click it so it has the keyboard and the mouse.
  walk   arrow keys or W/S; turn with Left/Right or the mouse; step sideways with A/D; hold Shift to run
  draw   hold Ctrl or the left mouse button while you walk on the canvas: the tiles you walk over turn blue
  READ   the right-hand switch south of the canvas: walk up to it and press Space or E. DOOM reads the digit in
         about 9 s of game time (35 tics/s) at --opt 3 and lights it on the display north of the canvas.
         --opt 3 changes one thing: an ACS script copies each layer's light levels into the next layer's gate heights, so every layer runs as one wave. --opt 0 reads in about 163 s. The check prints here once every doll and you stand still.
  CLEAR  the left-hand switch wipes the canvas. While DOOM reads (until the display lights), the pen, READ and
         CLEAR are off.
  quit   Esc frees the mouse (DOOM's menu; the game pauses), then close the window; or Ctrl+C here

